    "result_text": "The build succeeds and the test suite is green.\n\nLet me verify the full compile (main + generated DTO) didn't have hidden issues by confirming the whole thing built cleanly \u2014 the `BUILD SUCCESS` and generated `OwnerDto` (which the mapper auto-maps `memberId` from) confirm it. The work is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field. The suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1/1 test passing), and the audit log confirms the new format in action: `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1` = `NSW` + FY `27` + HASH8 `16E6609E` + Luhn CHK `1`.\n\n**What changed:**\n\n- **`AssignMemberId`** (new, replaces `AssignCustomerCode` + `AssignMembershipNumber`): builds `REGION + FY + HASH8`, appends a single Luhn check digit computed over that body's digits, and applies collision handling against existing `memberId`s (appending `-<n>`). HASH8 is the same SHA-256-over-(normalizedTelephone + lastName) first-8-upper-hex as before.\n- **`OwnerRegion`** (renamed from `CustomerCodeRegion`): derives the region straight from postcode/city (no separator to parse now). Deleted `CustomerCodeCheckDigit` (its Luhn is now the CHK segment, computed inline in `AssignMemberId`).\n- **`Owner` model** + **all 4 DB schema dialects**: replaced `customer_code`/`membership_number` columns and accessors with a single `member_id` (`VARCHAR(30)`/`TEXT`).\n- **`openapi.yml`**: removed `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, `membershipNumber`; added `memberId`; fixed the `locality` description. `fiscalYear`/`locality`/`timezone`/`ownerSegment` remain (unchanged spec).\n- **`OwnerMapper`**: dropped the `checkDigit` mapping, repointed `locality` to `OwnerRegion`; `memberId` is auto-mapped by name.\n- **`AuditOwnerCreated`**: both the human-readable line and the structured `OwnerCreatedEvent` record now carry `memberId`; `primaryIdentifier` returns it.\n- **`LocalityTimezone`** / **`OwnerSegment`**: repointed to `OwnerRegion`.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`**: the two steps collapsed into one `assignMemberId` step (still under the write transaction, still after `applyRegistrationDate` so the fiscal year is available).",
